# /auto_install.conf of the Deep32 Workstation medium: the GUIDED install. OpenBSD's own installer runs unattended
# with these answers (install.sub's _autorespond, extended by ship/install/patch-installsub.pl):
#   @SET:<field>@      the value from the settings disc (contract C7); without a settings disc, or without that
#                      field, it is asked on this machine's console
#   @ROOTDISK:<duid>@  the one empty disk of a VM when a settings disc is present; otherwise asked on the console
#   @ENCRYPT@          from the settings disc (absent: off for hw_profile vm, on for a real machine); without a
#                      settings disc it is asked on the console
#   @DEFAULT@          the installer's own default answer
#   @ASKSECRET@        typed twice on the console, never in a file (the disk passphrase only)
#   @DUID:<duid>@      the disk carrying that DUID (the install medium)
# No password is set here: both accounts stay locked until the first start sets them on the console.
# No secret and no person's value is in this file.
Choose your keyboard layout = @SET:keyboard@
System hostname = @SET:node_name@
Network interface to configure = done
DNS domain name = invalid
Password for root account = *************
Public ssh key for root account = none
Start sshd(8) by default = no
Do you expect to run the X Window System = yes
Do you want the X Window System to be started by xenodm(1) = no
Change the default console to com0 = no
Setup a user = @SET:user_name@
Full name for user = @DEFAULT@
Password for user = *************
Public ssh key for user = none
Allow root ssh login = no
What timezone are you in = @SET:time_zone@
Which disk is the root disk = @ROOTDISK:@MEDIA_DUID@@
Encrypt the root disk with a (p)assphrase or (k)eydisk = @ENCRYPT@
New passphrase = @ASKSECRET@
URL to autopartitioning template for disklabel = file:///@TEMPLATE@
Location of sets = disk
Is the disk partition already mounted = no
Which disk contains the install media = @DUID:@MEDIA_DUID@@
partition has the install sets = a
Pathname to the sets = 8.0/amd64
Set name(s) = -comp* -game* +site*
Checksum test for site80.tgz failed. Continue anyway = yes
Unverified sets: site80.tgz. Continue without verification = yes
